{
  "schema_version": "argument_graph/0.1",
  "example_id": "persuade:F3B4F60CE90C",
  "root": "w7",
  "units": [
    {
      "id": "w1",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 138,
      "text": "The Electoral colleg is a process in which the electors from the state pick the cannidate they want according to who has the popular vote.",
      "role": "lead",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w2",
      "start": 139,
      "end": 179,
      "text": "Which can also be a very biased process.",
      "role": "lead",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w3",
      "start": 180,
      "end": 239,
      "text": "The Electoral College is not registered or monitered enough",
      "role": "lead",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w4",
      "start": 240,
      "end": 312,
      "text": "because if an elector from the state wanted to pick who they want to win",
      "role": "lead",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w5",
      "start": 313,
      "end": 323,
      "text": "they could",
      "role": "lead",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w6",
      "start": 324,
      "end": 383,
      "text": "and there isn't really anything to stop them from doing so.",
      "role": "lead",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w7",
      "start": 385,
      "end": 440,
      "text": "We the people should do away with the Electoral College",
      "role": "position",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w8",
      "start": 441,
      "end": 508,
      "text": "and instead switch to a more regulated system like majority voting.",
      "role": "position",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w9",
      "start": 509,
      "end": 582,
      "text": "whichever cannidate that gets the most votes from the U.S. takes the win.",
      "role": "position",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w10",
      "start": 583,
      "end": 663,
      "text": "that way we wouldnt have to worry about our electors for the states being sneaky",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w11",
      "start": 664,
      "end": 699,
      "text": "because there wont be any electors.",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w12",
      "start": 700,
      "end": 757,
      "text": "State legislature is responsible for picking the electors",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w13",
      "start": 758,
      "end": 812,
      "text": "and the electors sometimes defy the will of the people",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w14",
      "start": 813,
      "end": 855,
      "text": "and cast the vote for who they want to win",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w15",
      "start": 856,
      "end": 930,
      "text": "just like when Richard Nixon only validated his opponets electors in 1960.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w16",
      "start": 931,
      "end": 987,
      "text": "The Electoral College would be a more just way of voting",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "conceded",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w17",
      "start": 988,
      "end": 1023,
      "text": "if the electors were well monitored",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w18",
      "start": 1024,
      "end": 1077,
      "text": "and if every state shared the same weight in the vote",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w19",
      "start": 1078,
      "end": 1115,
      "text": "but unfortunatley, it's not like that",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w20",
      "start": 1116,
      "end": 1149,
      "text": "so it needs to be done away with.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w21",
      "start": 1151,
      "end": 1225,
      "text": "The Electoral College is a unrestricted and very poorly regulated process,",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w22",
      "start": 1226,
      "end": 1258,
      "text": "and it is a very unfair process.",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w23",
      "start": 1259,
      "end": 1297,
      "text": "Because of the winner-take-all system.",
      "role": "claim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w24",
      "start": 1298,
      "end": 1344,
      "text": "In 1968, if 41,971 voters voted a diffrent way",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w25",
      "start": 1345,
      "end": 1385,
      "text": "the election would have been deadlocked.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w26",
      "start": 1386,
      "end": 1492,
      "text": "In 1976, if roughkly 5,500 voters in Ohio and about 3,600 voters in Hawaii had voted for a diffrent person",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w27",
      "start": 1493,
      "end": 1528,
      "text": "the election would have been a tie.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w28",
      "start": 1529,
      "end": 1609,
      "text": "And usually the bigger states are the only ones to actually see their cannidates",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w29",
      "start": 1610,
      "end": 1692,
      "text": "because the cannidates dont neccesarily visit states with very few electoral votes",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w30",
      "start": 1693,
      "end": 1728,
      "text": "because they wont help them as much",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w31",
      "start": 1729,
      "end": 1835,
      "text": "instead, they visit the \"swing states\", the states that have a bigger weight in the presidential election.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w32",
      "start": 1837,
      "end": 1961,
      "text": "However, on the other side the people that want to keep it are the ones that look at the few good things not the bad things.",
      "role": "counterclaim",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w33",
      "start": 1962,
      "end": 2141,
      "text": "Of those helpful things that comes with the electoral college is it majorly decreases the chance of a run-off election in which no cannidate receives a majority of the votes cast.",
      "role": "counterclaim",
      "stance": "conceded",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w34",
      "start": 2142,
      "end": 2200,
      "text": "The Electoral college also puts out a certainty of outcome",
      "role": "counterclaim",
      "stance": "conceded",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w35",
      "start": 2201,
      "end": 2327,
      "text": "because there is less likely to be a dispute over the outcome in a popular vote then a dispute over an Electoral College vote.",
      "role": "counterclaim",
      "stance": "reported",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w36",
      "start": 2329,
      "end": 2419,
      "text": "Of course, in life there is always at least some good in things like the Electoral College",
      "role": "concluding_summary",
      "stance": "conceded",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w37",
      "start": 2420,
      "end": 2470,
      "text": "but in this situation is does more harm then good.",
      "role": "concluding_summary",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w38",
      "start": 2471,
      "end": 2502,
      "text": "It is an overall unfair process",
      "role": "concluding_summary",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w39",
      "start": 2503,
      "end": 2539,
      "text": "because some states are less noticed",
      "role": "concluding_summary",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w40",
      "start": 2540,
      "end": 2584,
      "text": "because of how few electoral votes they hold",
      "role": "concluding_summary",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w41",
      "start": 2585,
      "end": 2676,
      "text": "and also because of the electors not being monitered on the vote they cast for their state.",
      "role": "concluding_summary",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w42",
      "start": 2677,
      "end": 2723,
      "text": "The Electoral College should be doen away with",
      "role": "concluding_summary",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    },
    {
      "id": "w43",
      "start": 2724,
      "end": 2833,
      "text": "and as a united country we shall adopt a more fair, equal , and all together well monitered system of voting.",
      "role": "concluding_summary",
      "stance": "endorsed",
      "polarity": "positive"
    }
  ],
